==Icelandic==

===Etymology===
From late {{etyl|non|is}} {{term|læra|lang=non}}, {{term|lǽra|lang=non}}, from {{etyl|osx|is}} {{term|lerian|lērian|lang=osx}}, ultimately from {{etyl|gem-pro|is}} {{recons|laizijaną|lang=gem-pro}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈlaiːra/|lang=is}}
*: {{rhymes|aiːra|lang=is}}

===Verb===
{{is-verb-weak|lærði|lært}}

# {{context|intransitive|lang=is}} to [[learn]], to [[study]]
#* Timothy 2:11-12 ([http://www.biblegateway.com/passage/?search=1+Timothy+2:11-12&version=NIV English], [http://www.biblegateway.com/passage/?search=1%20Timothy%202:11-12&version=ICELAND Icelandic])
#*: ''Konan á að '''læra''' í kyrrþey, í allri undirgefni. Ekki leyfi ég konu að kenna eða taka sér vald yfir manninum, heldur á hún að vera kyrrlát.''
#*:: A woman should '''learn''' in quietness and full submission. I do not permit a woman to teach or to have authority over a man; she must be silent.
# {{context|transitive|governs the accusative}} to [[study]] something, to [[learn]] something
#: ''Ég er að '''læra''' [[strjál stærðfræði|strjála stærðfræði]].''
#:: I'm '''studying''' [[discrete mathematics]].

====Conjugation====
{{is-conj-w2|l|æ|r}}

